<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Harran</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Harran is an ancient city in upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>, in present-day south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, known as a centre of the moon god Sin. After the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nineveh">Nineveh</a>, the last Assyrian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashur-uballit-ii">Ashur-uballit II</a> made a final stand there. Its capture by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonians">Babylonians</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medes">Medes</a> marked the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/harran.jpg" alt="Harran" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hamdigumus · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Harran_2015.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
